{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (automated cobbler orchestrator) submitted stitch task #5131 to extend cmd/sponge/main.go with four additional requirements from srd007-sponge:\n   - R2.4: Use lstat (not stat) to check if output path is a regular file; handle symlinks by writing directly instead of renaming\n   - R2.5: Ensure output file is never in a partially-written state (atomic fallback via temp-in-same-dir + rename)\n   - R3.1: Append mode (-a) prepends original file content before stdin content, including when stdin was spilled to a temp file\n   - R3.2: Append mode only applies when the output file already exists AND is a regular file\n   \n   Design decisions: extend existing main.go (don't rewrite), preserve existing R1.5/R2.1-R2.3 behavior.\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (go build), AC2 (go vet), AC3 (requirements implemented), AC4 (existing behavior preserved).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Sponge utility: reads all stdin before opening output file to prevent read-write pipeline conflicts\n   - lstat vs stat: lstat doesn't follow symlinks, needed to detect symlink output paths\n   - Atomic file writes via rename: rename is atomic on same filesystem; cross-device requires fallback\n   - Temp file spill: when stdin exceeds memory threshold, data is written to a temp file\n   - Signal cleanup: temp files cleaned up on SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP/SIGPIPE\n   - Differential testing pattern via pkg/testutils against Homebrew reference binaries\n   - SIGPIPE handler via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max per function (E8 constitution rule)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd007-sponge.yaml\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1-R6, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - Key requirements implemented: R2.4 (lstat regular file check), R2.5 (atomic output), R3.1 (append prepend), R3.2 (append only for regular files)\n     - Non-goals: no symlink following, no --buffer-size flag, no atomic writes for passthrough mode\n   \n   - cmd/sponge/main.go (MODIFIED - complete rewrite via Write tool)\n     - Extended from ~270 lines to ~310 lines\n     - Key changes made:\n       - `outputFileMode` renamed to `outputFileInfo`, returns 4 values: `(os.FileMode, bool, bool, error)` for mode, exists, isRegular, error\n       - `run` split into `run`, `runPassthrough`, `runOutput` to stay under 40-line limit\n       - New `prependOriginal` replaces `prependOriginalContent`, handles temp file spill case\n       - New `combineTempFiles` creates combined temp file with [original][stdin] when stdin was spilled\n       - New `appendFromFile` helper copies from source file to destination os.File\n       - `writeOutputFile` now accepts isRegular parameter, only attempts rename for regular files or new files (R2.4)\n       - New `atomicFallbackCopy` creates temp in same dir as output, copies, renames for atomicity (R2.5)\n       - New `directWrite` for non-regular files (symlinks, devices) - writes directly via OpenFile\n       - New `copyFileToWriter` helper for atomic fallback\n       - New `cleanupCurrentTempFile` for deferred global temp file cleanup\n       - Added `path/filepath` import for `filepath.Dir`\n       - Removed old `prependOriginalContent`, `fallbackCopy`, `cleanupTempFile(path)` functions\n\n     Complete written file (key new/changed functions):\n\n     ```go\n     // R2.4: use lstat to determine file existence, mode, and whether it is regular\n     func outputFileInfo(filename string) (os.FileMode, bool, bool, error) {\n         fi, err := sys.Lstat(filename)\n         if err != nil {\n             if os.IsNotExist(err) {\n                 return 0666, false, false, nil\n             }\n             return 0, false, false, fmt.Errorf(\"lstat %s: %w\", filename, err)\n         }\n         return fi.Mode.Perm(), true, fi.Mode.IsRegular(), nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n     ```go\n     func runOutput(filename string, data []byte, tmpFile string) int {\n         mode, exists, isRegular, err := outputFileInfo(filename)\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sponge: %v\\n\", err)\n             return 1\n         }\n         // R3.1, R3.2: append only when file exists and is a regular file\n         if *appendMode && exists && isRegular {\n             data, tmpFile, err = prependOriginal(filename, data, tmpFile)\n             if err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sponge: %v\\n\", err)\n                 return 1\n             }\n             if tmpFile != \"\" {\n                 setTempFile(tmpFile)\n             }\n         }\n         if err := writeOutputFile(filename, data, tmpFile, mode, exists, isRegular); err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sponge: %v\\n\", err)\n             return 1\n         }\n         clearTempFile()\n         return 0\n     }\n     ```\n\n     ```go\n     func prependOriginal(filename string, data []byte, tmpFile string) ([]byte, string, error) {\n         original, err := os.ReadFile(filename)\n         if err != nil {\n             return nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", filename, err)\n         }\n         if len(original) == 0 {\n             return data, tmpFile, nil\n         }\n         if tmpFile != \"\" {\n             combined, err := combineTempFiles(original, tmpFile)\n             if err != nil {\n                 return nil, \"\", err\n             }\n             return nil, combined, nil\n         }\n         combined := make([]byte, len(original)+len(data))\n         copy(combined, original)\n         copy(combined[len(original):], data)\n         return combined, \"\", nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n     ```go\n     func writeOutputFile(filename string, data []byte, tmpFile string, mode os.FileMode, exists bool, isRegular bool) error {\n         tmpPath := tmpFile\n         var err error\n         if tmpPath == \"\" {\n             tmpPath, err = spillToTempFile(data)\n             if err != nil {\n                 return err\n             }\n             setTempFile(tmpPath)\n         }\n         // R2.4: only attempt atomic rename for regular files or new files\n         if !exists || isRegular {\n             return attemptAtomicWrite(tmpPath, filename, mode, exists)\n         }\n         return directWrite(tmpPath, filename, mode)\n     }\n     ```\n\n     ```go\n     // R2.5: ensure output is never in a partially-written state\n     func atomicFallbackCopy(tmpPath, filename string, mode os.FileMode) error {\n         dir := filepath.Dir(filename)\n         tmpDst, err := os.CreateTemp(dir, \".sponge-\")\n         if err != nil {\n             return directWrite(tmpPath, filename, mode)\n         }\n         tmpDstPath := tmpDst.Name()\n         if err := copyFileToWriter(tmpPath, tmpDst, mode); err != nil {\n             os.Remove(tmpDstPath)\n             return err\n         }\n         if err := os.Rename(tmpDstPath, filename); err != nil {\n             os.Remove(tmpDstPath)\n             return directWrite(tmpPath, filename, mode)\n         }\n         os.Remove(tmpPath)\n         return nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No compilation or runtime errors encountered yet - the file was written but verification steps (go build, go vet) have not been run.\n   - Key design issue identified and fixed: the existing `prependOriginalContent` function didn't handle the temp-file spill case for append mode. When stdin was spilled to a temp file, `data` was nil, so `prependOriginalContent(filename, nil)` would return only the original content without the stdin data. Fixed by creating `prependOriginal` which accepts and returns both `data` and `tmpFile`, and creates a combined temp file when necessary.\n\n5. Prob